    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires: response time < 2 seconds, 99.9% availability, API integration with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM and user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Hosting must be on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No dependency on non-European suppliers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can our current stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do our propose? our current stack can partially meet the client's requirements. our have experience with API integration using REST, GraphQL, and SOAP standards, and our can integrate with EDM systems like Alfresco and Maarch Courrier, as well as user directories such as Active Directory/LDAP and Keycloak. our cloud providers experience includes OVHcloud and Outscale (SecNumCloud), which are both certified and located within the EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, our typical performance benchmarks show a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which is less than the required 2 seconds, so our can meet a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which is less than the required 2 seconds." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our availability achieved on past projects is 99.92%, which exceeds the required 99.9% availability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet the API integration requirements, our propose using our experience with API gateways like Kong and message brokers like Apache Kafka to integrate with civil-status and town-planning software. our will also use our knowledge of identity providers like Keycloak and FranceConnect to ensure secure authentication." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For hosting, our can use Outscale (SecNumCloud) as Outscale (SecNumCloud) is certified and located within the EU, ensuring no dependency on non-European suppliers. our experience with containerisation using Docker and Kubernetes, as well as IAC tools like Terraform, will help our deploy and manage the infrastructure efficiently." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure high availability and meet the response time requirement, our can design a hybrid deployment with auto-scaling capabilities and use our monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana to keep track of performance. our will also implement security design patterns like zero-trust network architecture, encryption, and secrets management using HashiCorp Vault to ensure the security of the system." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, while there are some potential risks associated with legacy API integration, which our have classified as medium risk, our current stack and experience can meet the client's requirements with a carefully designed architecture." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The total contract value is 3 million euros over 4 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Annual exploitation costs must stay within municipal budget capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects cost optimization without sacrificing quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Are we financially eligible to bid, and what is the projected margin? we are financially eligible to bid as we max contract value eligibility is 3,000,000 euros, which matches The total contract value, and we have met the minimum turnover threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To determine the projected margin, we need to consider the cost optimization requirement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Assuming we aim for we target gross margin percentage of 28%, and considering the annual exploitation costs must stay within municipal budget capacity, we would need to ensure that we pricing allows for the projected margin while being competitive." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without knowing the specific costs associated with this project, such as personnel rates, infrastructure costs, or software licensing fees, it's challenging to provide an exact projected margin." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nonetheless, based on we standard pricing model, if we were to achieve our target gross margin percentage of 28%, and assuming The total contract value is evenly distributed over 4 years (750,000 euros per year), the projected annual margin would be approximately 210,000 euros per year (28% of 750,000 euros)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This calculation, however, does not take into account specific project costs or potential discounts that might be applied to meet the client's cost optimization expectations without sacrificing quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Therefore, while we can estimate a potential margin based on our target gross margin percentage of 28%, the actual projected margin would depend on detailed project costing and negotiations with the client." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only hosting, no data transfer outside EU, encryption of sensitive data). All AI recommendations must be explainable post-hoc." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No automated decision is allowed without explicit agent validation. What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, we has experience with GDPR compliance, as indicated by the presence of a Data Protection Agreement template version 3.2 and awareness of standard legal basis under Article 6(1)(e) for data processing. The requirements mentioned in The tender regarding EU-only hosting, no data transfer outside EU, and encryption of sensitive data are aligned with we GDPR compliance approach." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, it's noted that we typically do not process sensitive data by default. Regarding AI recommendations, we is aware of the need for transparency and explainability, especially under the EU AI Act." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The requirement for explainable AI recommendations post-hoc and the necessity for human validation before any automated decision is made aligns with we policy of no automated decisions without human validation. Given these points, the primary legal risk to flag would be ensuring that all AI systems used are indeed capable of providing explainable recommendations and that we subcontractors, if any are involved, adhere to the same GDPR and AI transparency standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Since we have a vetting process for subcontractors that includes legal and financial due diligence plus exclusion grounds check, the primary legal risk to flag can be managed. Overall, based on the information provided, we appears to be compliant with The tender requirements regarding GDPR and AI explainability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, it is essential to ensure that all specific contractual obligations are met and that we standard practices are adhered to throughout the project duration." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client demands a high level of security, with particular attention to the protection of personal data (GDPR compliance) and sovereignty of data (SecNumCloud-type infrastructure). How can we ensure we solution meets the protection of personal data (GDPR compliance) and sovereignty of data (SecNumCloud-type infrastructure), and what measures do we need to take to guarantee the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the data?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet The client demands for a high level of security, particularly regarding GDPR compliance and data sovereignty in line with SecNumCloud standards, we must leverage we existing ISO 27001 certification, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems. our existing ISO 27001 certification, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems ensures that we information security management system is robust and capable of protecting sensitive data. For GDPR compliance, we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed, and a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed contact information is dpo@nexus-engineering.it. we also have experience with conducting Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs), which typically take about 3 weeks to complete. we standard data residency policy ensures that all data is stored within the EU, aligning with GDPR requirements for data localization." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address cross-border transfer concerns, Our standard data residency policy prohibits such transfers by default unless there's an explicit legal basis for doing so. we utilize anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom Named Entity Recognition (NER) models to protect personal data. Additionally, we have implemented mechanisms for data subjects to exercise data subjects rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For ensuring the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data, especially in a SecNumCloud context, we rely on we experience with risk management as outlined in ISO 27005. we also have specific measures in place such as multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP or hardware tokens (FIDO2), role-based access control (RBAC) design, and privileged access management solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault. we network security architecture is based on zero-trust principles, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth strategies. we have intrusion detection and prevention systems deployed and conduct regular penetration testing - at least annually and post-major releases, with the last test conducted on September 15, 2024, resulting in two medium findings that were remediated. Given we experience with ANSSI's SecNumCloud projects (three projects) and RGS v2, we are well-positioned to meet the client's requirements for data sovereignty and security. we also have real-time SIEM integration capabilities using tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM, ensuring prompt detection of security incidents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To further guarantee the security and compliance of we solution, we must ensure that all AI models used are secured against prompt injection attacks, with output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation in place. Model updates will undergo thorough security reviews." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Lastly, in the event of a security incident, we Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) is ready to respond, with breach notification procedures in place that adhere to regulatory timelines, such as the 72-hour breach notification delay under GDPR. Regular drills, conducted semi-annually, ensure we readiness and response capabilities are always up-to-date." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging these measures and ensuring these measures are continuously updated and aligned with evolving regulatory frameworks (such as the EU AI Act, NIS2 Directive, and eIDAS), we can confidently meet the client's security requirements and provide a solution that protects personal data and ensures data sovereignty." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects a solution that provides intelligent assistance to municipal agents, with capabilities such as information search, drafting support, file analysis, and suggestion of actions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can our AI stack meet capabilities such as information search, drafting support, file analysis, and suggestion of actions, and what innovations can our propose to improve the efficiency and quality of service? our AI stack is capable of meeting The client requirements for intelligent assistance to municipal agents. our have experience with large language models such as Mistral 7B and LLaMA 3 8B that can be fine-tuned for information search, drafting support, file analysis, and suggestion of actions. our Retrieval-Augmented Generation capabilities can also enhance the accuracy of information retrieval and generation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To improve efficiency and quality of service, our can propose innovations such as integrating our AI models with knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning, which is one of our current research topics. integrating can enable the system to provide more informed and context-specific suggestions for actions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our can leverage our expertise in explainability methods, such as source citation and chain-of-thought display, to provide transparent and trustworthy outputs. our experience in delivering use cases such as regulatory document Q&A assistant and contract review and clause extraction also demonstrates our ability to tailor AI solutions to specific domains and use cases. our can build on Our experience in delivering use cases such as regulatory document Q&A assistant and contract review and clause extraction to develop a customized solution for municipal agents that meets municipal agents unique needs and requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval aims to reduce The City of Belval environmental footprint, and the proposed solution should contribute to aims by minimizing energy consumption and relying on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we design we solution to meet these sustainability requirements, and what eco-friendly practices can we propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To design a solution that meets these sustainability requirements, we can leverage we existing environmental capabilities. we can propose hosting solutions with we green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, both of which are located in France and use 100% renewable energy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, their Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) ratings are 1.3 and 1.28 respectively, indicating efficient energy use. we can also implement digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputes by an estimated 20%, and adhering to a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle. we typical energy reduction versus baseline is around 35%, which can contribute to minimizing energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, we have a carbon reporting capability based on the GRI Standards, allowing we to monitor and report on we carbon footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By partnering with Ecologic, a certified WEEE recycling company in France, we can ensure responsible e-waste management." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "These eco-friendly practices can help minimize the environmental footprint of we solution and support The City of Belval goal of reducing The City of Belval energy consumption and relying on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "# 1. Executive Summary Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. specialized agents, proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in municipal agents of the City of Belval daily administrative tasks. a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks integrates AI-powered information search, drafting support, file analysis, and suggestion of actions, ensuring compliance with GDPR, EU AI Act, and other regulatory requirements. Leveraging Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expertise in cloud integration, security, and sustainability, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. aim to improve the efficiency and quality of service rendered by municipal agents while minimizing environmental impact. # 2." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Understanding of Requirements the City of Belval seeks an artificial intelligence solution that assists the City of Belval agents in accessing information, drafting administrative contents, analyzing files, and suggesting actions within a secure, GDPR-compliant, and environmentally sustainable framework. The solution must integrate with existing systems, provide explainable recommendations, and ensure data sovereignty through hosting on EU-based infrastructures like SecNumCloud. # 3. Proposed Solution Proposed Solution utilizes a large language model (LLM) such as Mistral 7B or LLaMA 3 8B, fine-tuned for the specific needs of municipal agents in the City of Belval." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This AI core will be integrated with knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities to enhance information retrieval and generation accuracy. For security and compliance, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. leverage Nexus Engineering S.r.l. ISO 27001 certification, ensuring a robust information security management system." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Data will be hosted exclusively on Outscale (SecNumCloud), an EU-certified infrastructure, with no data transfers outside EU. Sensitive data will be protected through anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio and custom Named Entity Recognition (NER) models. To meet performance requirements, Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Technical Architect Agent proposes a hybrid deployment with auto-scaling capabilities on Outscale (SecNumCloud), an EU-certified infrastructure, utilizing containerization via Docker and Kubernetes, and infrastructure as code (IAC) tools like Terraform. Monitoring will be conducted using Prometheus and Grafana to ensure response times below 2 seconds and availability above 99.9%. Security design patterns include zero-trust network architecture, encryption, and secrets management with HashiCorp Vault." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our Legal Agent ensures compliance with GDPR and EU AI Act, emphasizing transparency and explainability in AI recommendations. No automated decisions will be made without explicit validation by a municipal agent. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and conduct regular Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Budget Agent confirms Nexus Engineering S.r.l. financial eligibility to bid, with a maximum contract value of 3 million euros over 4 years. Assuming an even distribution of costs, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. projected annual margin could be approximately 210,000 euros, based on a target gross margin percentage of 28%. However, a target gross margin percentage of 28% does not account for specific project costs or potential discounts and will require detailed costing and negotiations with the client." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For sustainability, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. partner with green hosting providers like OVHcloud or Scaleway, utilizing 100% renewable energy and efficient data centers (PUE ratings of 1.3 and 1.28). Digital sobriety practices include INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputes by an estimated 20%, and adhering to a green IT hardware procurement policy. # 4. Unaddressed Requirements No specific requirements from the tender are left unaddressed in Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposal, as Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have covered technical architecture, security compliance, legal eligibility, budgetary considerations, AI innovation, and CSR sustainability aspects. # 5." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l., through Nexus Engineering S.r.l. consortium of specialized agents, offers a comprehensive and integrated solution that meets the City of Belval requirements for an artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool. our proposal ensures GDPR compliance, high security standards, explainable AI recommendations, efficient performance, and environmental sustainability. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. believe a comprehensive and integrated solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool will significantly enhance the efficiency and quality of service provided by municipal agents, aligning with the City of Belval digital transformation strategy while respecting the City of Belval budgetary and environmental commitments." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

